Local timestamped streaming for an application on the Pluto itself: uri=local: with direct=1 or
local_timestamp=1 (NexusBS) and timestamp_every=N uses the FPGA's timestamped DMA blocks in place,
without the USB/UDP SDR gadgets, threads or queues (PlutoSDR_LocalTS); same stream semantics as the
gadget streamers. For every timestamped stream (gadgets too) the tick unit is the requested sample
rate, not the AD9361's rounded readback (599999 for 600000 drifted a sample per second against the
plan). Also: timestamp_every must be even; TX setSampleRate used the RX decimation flag; the stream
mutex blocks instead of spinning (a waiter burned a core while a stream waited for data); streams
are released before the IIO context in the device destructor.

